{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508001-eye-of-hazimel","id":1508001,"title":"Eye of Hazimel","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-04-10T23:36:56-07:00","id":1508001,"title":"Eye of Hazimel","content":"In your opinion, would an elder vampire with the Eye of Hazimel be able to destroy a powerful Methuselah like Ur-Shulgi/Mithras/Baba Yaga?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-11T00:22:19-07:00","id":1508003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508001-eye-of-hazimel#post1508001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In your opinion, would an elder vampire with the Eye of Hazimel be able to destroy a powerful Methuselah like Ur-Shulgi/Mithras/Baba Yaga?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mithras? Maybe.<br /> Ur-Shulgi and Baba Yaga, who might be in the same tier or even older and versed in blood sorcery than Hazimel himself? I have serious doubts, honestly.<br /> <br /> Unless you think of the Eye as a sort of power amplifier macguffin that is wholy independent for its magic on Hazimel's own capabilities.<br /> If one works from such an interpretation of the artifact i'd say what it can or not do is completely up to ST fiat.<br /> <br /> That said, if it were the case, i'd imagine Hazimel himself (along with many methuselahs) would make a more direct effort to recover it, since the idea of something that further amplifies a <b><i>methuselah</i></b>'s own power is simply mind-boggling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 04-11-2023, 03:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-11T01:39:44-07:00","id":1508008,"title":"","content":"Even Mithras is a bit questionable<br /> But more questionable, the usage of the Eye<br /> Elder vampires are powerhungry, yes, but I think would need a very good reason to use something as shady as the Eye of Hazimel<br /> Probbaly after careful consideration, would use a child or a fledgeling blood bonded to hell, to see the effects<br /> The lore behind the Eye is fragmented as best<br /> <br /> Not much is known about Hazimel, only that he originated in India and was a rebellious childe that left his sire after an undefined period of time.<br /> Rumors tell that he was a stonemason in life who used his Eye as a method of control over various rulers. The Ravnos claim that he was born &quot;far to the North&quot; and served originally as a guardian of a goddess dedicated to combating the asuratizayya (Kuei-jin). The asuratizayya eventually retaliated against her by turning Hazimel against her, causing him to kill her. Insane with grief, he ripped out his own eye and fled into the mountains, where he was discovered by Zapathasura.<br /> When the Antediluvian offered him vengeance, Hazimel accepted, forsaking his name for the title &quot;Rakshasa&quot;. He is said to have bared his Eye as a nazar (amulet - a nazar - meaning 'sight', 'surveillance', 'attention', and other related concepts - is an eye-shaped amulet believed to protect against the evil eye.), which allowed him to see through falsehoods.<br /> The Karavalashina Vrana records that the Rakshasa became war-weary and confronted his sire with this. The two clashed and the Rakshasa became Zapathasura's second-greatest enemy, supposed to have cast his lot with one of his greater nemeses like Ennoia. In some versions of the story, he left India for either Africa or the Middle Kingdom, while in others, Zapathasura took his Eye from him and imprisoned him until he would repent. Other sources claim that he was betrayed by Ravana after the latter turned to infernalism, because his eye could see through his deceptions. In later centuries, Hazimel became a forgotten entity, entirely referred to by his epithet.<br /> In V20, Beckett reunites Hazimel with his Eye. In return, the Methuselah chooses him as his deliverer, imparting him with knowledge of long dead Indus scripts. Hazimel reunites with Chandraputra in renewing combat against the asurazitayya and Ravana who is rumored be behind their new activity.<br /> <br /> Now I think any self respecting Elder would avoid using such thing<br /> But lets supose they would use it; the Eye of Hazimel is a bit like the One Ring of Sauron; Hazimel poured some of his might in to it, but eventually could see thrugh the Eye and affect the bearer<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-11T04:08:07-07:00","id":1508015,"title":"","content":"Depends on the elder build and the methusaleah. All vampires become strong with age but that has a limit, what truly makes you powerful is how you use your time and your potential.<br /> <br /> Some high tier elders can compete or defeat low tier metusaleah in combat, For example, Tyler or Patricia of Bollinbrook would totally destroy Critias despite a difference in age above 1.000 years. The only thing stopping her is the fear of a blood hunt,<br /> <br /> Not every vampire elder/meth is a powerhouse, some survive so long by hidding/avoiding the game, being pollitically cunning or having a strong net of allies/subordinates. Also torpor is a thing, age is not enough, you need to be active to develop your powers.<br /> <br /> Now about the Eye of Hazimel in my desk it provides powers based on the mythology of the India, it is a very powerful artifact but how far it will take you depends on your base stats and how well it synergizes with what the eye provides to you.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-11T05:04:33-07:00","id":1508018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508001-eye-of-hazimel?p=1508008#post1508008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even Mithras is a bit questionable<br /> But more questionable, the usage of the Eye</div> </div> </div> </div>True, in both instances.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508001-eye-of-hazimel?p=1508008#post1508008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Elder vampires are powerhungry, yes, but I think would need a very good reason to use something as shady as the Eye of Hazimel</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but then the same could be said of &quot;doing the Antediluvians' work/serving the 2nd Generation&quot; and yet we have several secret societies wholy centered around that exact utterly shady conceit.<br /> <br /> I can definitely see some ancillae and elders, Ravnos or not, in India or neighboring countries with peculiar takes on the matter of Hazimel's history, identity and motives - backed by myths, literature and more even - that might see a direct link with the ancient as a plus instead of a con, not to go into weird theories and experiments that would make Hesha's idea in BJD of twisting blood sympathies on the Eye to make into a sort of compass to tracking down Set (or other Antes, depending on the clan of the user) seem tame by comparison.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508001-eye-of-hazimel?p=1508008#post1508008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The lore behind the Eye is fragmented as best<br /> <br /> Not much is known about Hazimel, only that he originated in India and was a rebellious childe that left his sire after an undefined period of time.<br /> Rumors tell that he was a stonemason in life who used his Eye as a method of control over various rulers. The Ravnos claim that he was born &quot;far to the North&quot; and served originally as a guardian of a goddess dedicated to combating the asuratizayya (Kuei-jin). The asuratizayya eventually retaliated against her by turning Hazimel against her, causing him to kill her. Insane with grief, he ripped out his own eye and fled into the mountains, where he was discovered by Zapathasura.<br /> When the Antediluvian offered him vengeance, Hazimel accepted, forsaking his name for the title &quot;Rakshasa&quot;. He is said to have bared his Eye as a nazar (amulet - a nazar - meaning 'sight', 'surveillance', 'attention', and other related concepts - is an eye-shaped amulet believed to protect against the evil eye.), which allowed him to see through falsehoods.<br /> The Karavalashina Vrana records that the Rakshasa became war-weary and confronted his sire with this. The two clashed and the Rakshasa became Zapathasura's second-greatest enemy, supposed to have cast his lot with one of his greater nemeses like Ennoia. In some versions of the story, he left India for either Africa or the Middle Kingdom, while in others, Zapathasura took his Eye from him and imprisoned him until he would repent. Other sources claim that he was betrayed by Ravana after the latter turned to infernalism, because his eye could see through his deceptions. In later centuries, Hazimel became a forgotten entity, entirely referred to by his epithet.<br /> In V20, Beckett reunites Hazimel with his Eye. In return, the Methuselah chooses him as his deliverer, imparting him with knowledge of long dead Indus scripts. Hazimel reunites with Chandraputra in renewing combat against the asurazitayya and Ravana who is rumored be behind their new activity.<br /> <br /> Now I think any self respecting Elder would avoid using such thing<br /> But lets supose they would use it; the Eye of Hazimel is a bit like the One Ring of Sauron; Hazimel poured some of his might in to it, but eventually could see thrugh the Eye and affect the bearer</div> </div> </div> </div>Not exactly, depending on how one interpret the tales - what if instead of Hazimel, the power within the Eye comes instead of <i>the curse of the asuratizayya</i> upon him or even of <b>the dead goddess that he once served and betrayed</b> before gouging his own eye in grief, even before his embrace?<br /> It's a <b>very</b> slippery slope indeed that one....\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 04-11-2023, 05:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-11T20:00:56-07:00","id":1508111,"title":"","content":"Many interesting responses here, especially regarding the story and possibilities of the Eye of Hazimel. One thing, one naturally thinks when talking about artifacts, is the equivalent powers such artifact would give the character. I remember once someone here in the forums mentioned that the Eye of Hazimel would grant Chimerstry 9, Koldunic Sorcery 9 and Vicissitude 9 in their games, to anyone using the Eye. Also, that it would give Hazimel ways to see the current owner and influence his actions in a way similar to &quot;The One Ring&quot; in LOTR.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-11T22:20:16-07:00","id":1508114,"title":"","content":"I don't see this as a mechanical issue. The Eye of Hazimel is a plot device. It can do whatever the ST wants it to do. Methuselahs, by and large, are also plot devices. They do whatever the ST wants them to do. So the question of an elder using the one to destroy the other is also a plot device - it can happen if the ST wants it to. Does it present an interesting scenario for the PCs? If yes, then go with it. If not, ignore it.<br /> <br /> I, personally, am not a fan of the Revised era metaplot so the actual question is meaningless in my own chronicles. None of the Revised metaplot exists in my chronicles. But I do have similar artifacts in my chronicles, like I explained <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445128-vampire-relic-the-eye-of-the-all-high\">here</a>. At the end of the day, it is just a question of what I want to happen in my chronicle and if I feel the flavor text will justify it in the minds of the PCs.<br /> <br /> Not very helpful, I know. Because I think the Eye of Hazimel is a pretty crappy artifact, I'll say &quot;no&quot;. But in terms of what it was supposed to be able to do in the badly written clan novels, then the answer would be &quot;yes.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-11T23:26:41-07:00","id":1508116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't see this as a mechanical issue. The Eye of Hazimel is a plot device. It can do whatever the ST wants it to do. Methuselahs, by and large, are also plot devices. They do whatever the ST wants them to do. So the question of an elder using the one to destroy the other is also a plot device - it can happen if the ST wants it to. Does it present an interesting scenario for the PCs? If yes, then go with it. If not, ignore it. </div> </div> </div>I understand that many Storytellers like to use the plot device approach to many things, but for different reasons I like to have a full picture of what something or someone can and cannot do. First, we're playing this chronicle for centuries, we started in 1200 and we are in 1500, so the PCs are all elders already, with considerable power, ones mainly political, others have more &quot;surviving tools&quot;, etc. So, the gap of power between a Methuselah and the group as a whole isn't that huge, that's one of the main reasons I make a complete character sheet to most important characters in the story. Second, there are many players who prefer this approach or who outright think it's &quot;unfair&quot; for the Storyteller to simply use the &quot;plot device card&quot;, to know that there are specific limits in what a certain character can and/or cannot do. All in all, if a character is an important part of the story, I make his complete character sheet.<br /> <br /> I think about the Eye in the same way. I want to decide exactly what it can and what it can't do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I, personally, am not a fan of the Revised era metaplot so the actual question is meaningless in my own chronicles. None of the Revised metaplot exists in my chronicles. But I do have similar artifacts in my chronicles, like I explained <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445128-vampire-relic-the-eye-of-the-all-high\">here</a>. At the end of the day, it is just a question of what I want to happen in my chronicle and if I feel the flavor text will justify it in the minds of the PCs.\u200b </div> </div> </div>Oh, very good! I've read the thread and it inspired me a great deal. Actualy &quot;Eye of Odin&quot; sounds very interesting and it's a name much easier to catch the player's mind, as even if we're not sure about what kind of creature Odin was, we all have an idea of what Odin means, unlike Hazimel (that about half my players can't seem to agree on a way to pronounce it and everytime they do it differently than the last time lol).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not very helpful, I know. Because I think the Eye of Hazimel is a pretty crappy artifact, I'll say &quot;no&quot;. But in terms of what it was supposed to be able to do in the badly written clan novels, then the answer would be &quot;yes.&quot; </div> </div> </div>I'm not one to judge, I quite like the idea of this kind of artifact as it spices up stories, especially when it has potential cursess/and/or problems associated with it and it's a part of another &quot;blood god&quot;. So you'd say that according to the novel it would be able to make an Elder able to destroy a Methuselah or do you agree with the powers people mention that it should grant?<br /> <br /> By the way, thanks for contributing to the discussion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T10:00:31-07:00","id":1509208,"title":"","content":"I'm drawing a blank on what the Eye Of Hazimel did power wise? I know it jacked up a neonate to insane levels that he seriously hurt a gathering of Gangrel including Xavier because it possessed a measure of an ancient 4th generation Ravnos might. I forgot what were the things that &quot;Leopold&quot; did when he was using it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T21:09:06-07:00","id":1509250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508001-eye-of-hazimel?p=1508111#post1508111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Many interesting responses here, especially regarding the story and possibilities of the Eye of Hazimel. One thing, one naturally thinks when talking about artifacts, is the equivalent powers such artifact would give the character. I remember once someone here in the forums mentioned that the Eye of Hazimel would grant Chimerstry 9, Koldunic Sorcery 9 and Vicissitude 9 in their games, to anyone using the Eye. Also, that it would give Hazimel ways to see the current owner and influence his actions in a way similar to &quot;The One Ring&quot; in LOTR.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, to be honest from what i remember of Leopold's battle with Xaviar's posse i'd actually say more Chimerstry, Koldunic Sorcery &amp; Vicissitude 6-7, but then i work on a &quot;if you can't raze a city with Thaumaturgy 7 like Menele did Pompeii &amp; Herculanum, you're doing it wrong&quot; scale in my own games. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> As an aside, i've been sketching out something of a &quot;BJD chronicle&quot; for some time and one of the things i've messed up with is the &quot;False Caine&quot; of Berlin - that in my chronicle is ALSO the &quot;cabbie Caine&quot; from LA in Bloodlines - and i've been of late toying with the idea of merging the Eye with the Bane Mummy artifacts empowering (and maddening) Ankla Hotep. Still uncertain, lots of lore and metaplot tweaks to account for before getting even near to that, but it's an idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 04-22-2023, 12:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T22:56:47-07:00","id":1509255,"title":"","content":"It granted Leopold great power over Chimerstry and PERHAPS Vicissitude <br /> I'm not convinced about the later<br /> He destroyed an entire revel of Gangrel on the outskirts of New York, summoning the fire beneath the earth itself to subjugate his mighty attackers. - either Chimestry or Koldunic sorcery or god knows what - tho' I suspect it was reality warping via Lv7. <b>Suspension of Disbelief</b> (Make an illusion seem completely real or what is real seem unbelievable), Lv8. <b>Occlusion/Synesthesia</b> (Control how a single target's or group's senses work), Lv8 <b>Sensory Overload </b>(Incapacitate a target by overstimulating their senses) and <b>Visions from the Asura</b> (Assault a target with constant illusions, making it nearly impossible to know what is real or not)<br /> With reality warping it is easy to swat a Revel of anoying Gangrel away, it seems big and scrary, but a don't forget, it was in New York, and in the New World, powerfull and ancient means different; take the strongest of the team for example; Xavier de Calais. The Justicar was not even 700 years old... born around 1320 and embraced 1356. Powerfull, yes. But compared to a real Methuselah, a fourth or fifth Generation elder who has existed for at least a millennium? Rookie.<br /> <br /> Leopold later collected the remains of the defeated Gangrel and created a gargantuan sculpture stretched in every direction at every angle to almost fill a very sizable cavern nearby. The work was not only of stone; flesh and bone adorned the sculpture and were incorporated into it. Entombed within the work were kindred limbs, the bodies of a dozen or more, few completely intact, some still moving. Leopold considered that abomination to be his masterpiece and subsequently went into torpor for weeks.<br /> <br /> Many interpret it Leopold had vicissitude, but I'm not that sure. Hazimel never really showed any sign if taint or realtionship with the Tzimisce...<br /> I think it was the lvl9 power, <b>Mayaparisatya </b>- Temporarily make an illusion completely real <b>or alter a person or object that already exists</b>, possibly even erasing them from existence<br /> Fit more in the &quot;theme&quot;, not to mention Hazimel was - as rumors tell - a stonemason in life who used his Eye as a method of control over various rulers. Leopold was a sculptor, a Toreador one (well he thought he was one, and we all know Toreador are closer to the pleasures of life and flesh...) and in his insanity, the two thing met. <br /> <br /> While Leopold slept, the Setite took the Eye and left. Leopold woke up to find his &quot;vision&quot; was gone and began looking for it, as the Novel describes it; so I think the Eye gave him Auspex<br /> ...and from Leopold lingering insanity, the Auspex and Chimestry brought out a latent Dementation<br /> <br /> TLDR<br /> I would say the Eye gave Leopold at least level <b>9 Chimerstry</b> (what a 4th Gen Hazimel would have...)<br /> <b>Auspex</b> (&quot;he called it Vision&quot;)<br /> <b>Fortitude</b> (he took quite a beating, but to be honest, not many Gangrel got close to land a hit on him, so this is speculation)<br /> And maybe he developed a nice <b>Dementation</b><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-22T08:32:25-07:00","id":1509280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> i work on a &quot;if you can't raze a city with Thaumaturgy 7 like Menele did Pompeii &amp; Herculanum, you're doing it wrong&quot; scale in my own games. </div> </div> </div>To be honest, I do the same in my games lol. I have the impression the combination of Disciplines <i>Jaws of the Dracon</i> (that can basically nuke a city with a mystical storm of pure elemental destruction) was created thinking about what Menele did with his level of Thaumaturgy, because it requires level 7 Blood Sorcery. In any case, then we have to consider the &quot;balance factor&quot; (or the lack thereof in the WoD), but to boost the artifact's appeal I'd be willing to make it more powerful (and dangerous), but that's because the chronicle I'm ST is currently an elder story.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As an aside, i've been sketching out something of a &quot;BJD chronicle&quot; for some time and one of the things i've messed up with is the &quot;False Caine&quot; of Berlin - that in my chronicle is ALSO the &quot;cabbie Caine&quot; from LA in Bloodlines - and i've been of late toying with the idea of merging the Eye with the Bane Mummy artifacts empowering (and maddening) Ankla Hotep. Still uncertain, lots of lore and metaplot tweaks to account for before getting even near to that, but it's an idea. </div> </div> </div>That's a very interesting idea, I used this story or should I say, I rather adapted some of its elements into a medieval story in one of my games, but then instead of Caine, the artifact made the Cainite look like Michael, the Patriarch, so it made a lot of his followers think he &quot;resurrected&quot;, it was quite interesting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> but a don't forget, it was in New York, and in the New World, powerfull and ancient means different; take the strongest of the team for example; Xavier de Calais. </div> </div> </div>Yes, even though Xavier is a powerhouse in the New World, he's far from being a powerful Methuselah, compared to Mithras/Goratrix/Michael/Ur-Shulgi/Baba Yaga etc, he's just a &quot;funny little pooch&quot;. So, one can say that perhaps this had a huge influence in the Camarilla not taking his warning that seriously. <br /> <br /> I also think that given Hazimel's lineage and origin, etc, it would be much more fitting to make the item give powers that are somehow related to the Ravnos, but I'm thinking about making the artifact's origin a bit more hazy. In the chronicle I mentioned it has only been mentioned by some NPCs, so I can still make my final decision about its real powers.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-22T09:25:30-07:00","id":1509288,"title":"","content":"That was some very impressive stuff that Leopold was able to with the Eye and think what someone like Hesha who is older and somewhat more powerful then the Toreador if he was inclined.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-22T09:30:11-07:00","id":1509291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508001-eye-of-hazimel#post1508001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In your opinion, would an elder vampire with the Eye of Hazimel be able to destroy a powerful Methuselah like Ur-Shulgi/Mithras/Baba Yaga?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that they would be taken off guard by the power an elder like Hesha or my Brujah character's grandsire could do with it. But in the end potent methuselahs like Ashrad, Baba Yaga, Mithras, and Ur-Shulgi would draw upon there vast amount of experience and power and defeat the upstart. Experience and cunning will always beat raw power in most instances.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-22T11:21:31-07:00","id":1509304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508001-eye-of-hazimel?p=1509291#post1509291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that they would be taken off guard by the power an elder like Hesha or my Brujah character's grandsire could do with it. But in the end potent methuselahs like Ashrad, Baba Yaga, Mithras, and Ur-Shulgi would draw upon there vast amount of experience and power and defeat the upstart. Experience and cunning will always beat raw power in most instances.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I'd also be inclined to say the Methuselah would likely have the upper hand, although after that ridiculous situation where Theo Bell (&quot;a little baby&quot; in terms of Cainite power) was able to kill Hardestadt with a shotgun (!!!) I'd say it depends on the writer lol, at the very least the Eye of Hazimel would make such a situation much more believable than a damn shotgun that most ancient vampires would laugh at. The thing is that with most of these powerful Methuselah, the likes of Mithras, Baba Yaga, Goratrix, etc, it would be extremely hard for the vampire to be directly in front of them in the first place, so they would likely have plenty of ways to deal with such an upstart. And sure, cunning and experience would almost always topple raw power, especially that in the cases of the Cainites I mentioned, they have not only experience and cunning but also a huge deal of raw power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-23T10:12:56-07:00","id":1509391,"title":"","content":"That is given that most of them are direct childer of their antediluvian and that is a considerable amount of power to have in general. I should add that the fact that these kindred have survived for thousands of years is a testament to there cunning. <br /> <br /> I think that an elder with the Eye would have a hard time taking down Siegfried the Prince of Vancouver, sure he lacks the raw power of the others that been noted. But he is no pushover and has been around since the late 4th century and is well versed in his disciplines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 04-23-2023, 01:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-23T10:28:50-07:00","id":1509395,"title":"","content":"I hope that future books will cover how Theo Bell a 9th generation ancilla took down a 6th generation elder with a dragon breath shotgun and got away intact and why the Camarilla leadership hasn\u2019t put him on the red list.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-23T17:16:56-07:00","id":1509419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508001-eye-of-hazimel#post1508001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In your opinion, would an elder vampire with the Eye of Hazimel be able to destroy a powerful Methuselah like Ur-Shulgi/Mithras/Baba Yaga?</div> </div> </div> </div>No.<br /> <br /> But I talked with Justin Achilli and the Eye of Hazmiel is basically just a device for channeling Hazmiel's power.<br /> <br /> Which is to say it's like Frodo with the One Ring vs. Sauron.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-23T17:22:08-07:00","id":1509420,"title":"","content":"It pays to have friends in the right places.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-23T23:15:01-07:00","id":1509450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508001-eye-of-hazimel?p=1509395#post1509395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope that future books will cover how Theo Bell a 9th generation ancilla took down a 6th generation elder with a dragon breath shotgun and got away intact and why the Camarilla leadership hasn\u2019t put him on the red list.</div> </div> </div> </div>We actually have an answer for that, which is that Marcus Vitel was faking his death.<br /> <br /> Even so, we have Cristof there and Cristof has the Sword of the Dracon and has also killed 5th generation Methusaleh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-24T08:48:33-07:00","id":1509479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508001-eye-of-hazimel?p=1509450#post1509450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We actually have an answer for that, which is that Marcus Vitel was faking his death.<br /> <br /> Even so, we have Cristof there and Cristof has the Sword of the Dracon and has also killed 5th generation Methusaleh.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't Cristof older and a more potent generation then Bell? I'm not overly knowledgeable about him in general and he kind of sounds interesting from the few mentions of him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-24T10:11:19-07:00","id":1509488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508001-eye-of-hazimel?p=1509419#post1509419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No.<br /> <br /> But I talked with Justin Achilli and the Eye of Hazmiel is basically just a device for channeling Hazmiel's power.<br /> <br /> Which is to say it's like Frodo with the One Ring vs. Sauron.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see, but the One Ring with Frodo only allowed him to become invisible if I remember correctly (It's been a while since I don't read the book), while it in the hands of Gandalf or Galadriel it would give them godlike powers. If the Eye of Hazimel allows one to channel Hazimel's powers it would be nearly correct to assume that it would give the wearer to potentially channel the powers we were talking about, i.e. Chimerstry 9, etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I hope that future books will cover how Theo Bell a 9th generation ancilla took down a 6th generation elder with a dragon breath shotgun and got away intact and why the Camarilla leadership hasn\u2019t put him on the red list. </div> </div> </div>I'd also say I hope it, but I think it's unlikely to get any satisfactory answer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Isn't Cristof older and a more potent generation then Bell? I'm not overly knowledgeable about him in general and he kind of sounds interesting from the few mentions of him. </div> </div> </div>Cristof was embraced in 1194, so in the modern setting he would be more than 8 centuries old, so yes, he's WAY OUT Theo Bell's league and also he owns the <i>Ainkurn Sword</i>, that makes him really dangerous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12348,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","user":"Herr Meister","date":". 04-24-2023, 01:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-24T15:38:47-07:00","id":1509529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508001-eye-of-hazimel?p=1509488#post1509488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cristof was embraced in 1194, so in the modern setting he would be more than 8 centuries old, so yes, he's WAY OUT Theo Bell's league and also he owns the <i>Ainkurn Sword</i>, that makes him really dangerous.</div> </div> </div> </div>800 years that he spent about maybe 795 in Torpor, though.<br /> <br /> The rest he spent slaughtering vampires, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/d