inkurn Sword</i>, that makes him really dangerous.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-24T15:48:29-07:00","id":1509532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508001-eye-of-hazimel?p=1509529#post1509529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 800 years that he spent about maybe 795 in Torpor, though.<br /> <br /> The rest he spent slaughtering vampires, though.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh, I thought my post bugged somehow, sorry. Yes, there's that (although it isn't clear how much time he spent in torpor), but as I said, the fact that he owns an important &quot;Plot item&quot; make it much more believable to see him killing an ancient vampire, besides Vampire Redemption was a video game,also one of the reasons why it isn't very clear how much time has passed in game, because the impression the game gives us is that a lot of time passes while we're playing with him, the travel to Vienna, the come back, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-24T19:26:57-07:00","id":1509543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508001-eye-of-hazimel?p=1509532#post1509532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Oh, I thought my post bugged somehow, sorry. Yes, there's that (although it isn't clear how much time he spent in torpor), but as I said, the fact that he owns an important &quot;Plot item&quot; make it much more believable to see him killing an ancient vampire, besides Vampire Redemption was a video game,also one of the reasons why it isn't very clear how much time has passed in game, because the impression the game gives us is that a lot of time passes while we're playing with him, the travel to Vienna, the come back, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>True enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T12:19:48-07:00","id":1509608,"title":"","content":"So what generation is Christoff?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T12:30:59-07:00","id":1509612,"title":"","content":"<b>Christof Romuald</b>\u200b was Embraced by Ecaterina the Wise, in Prague during the Dark Ages. She was originally an eighth generation vampire, but committed diablerie in the late 20th century.<br /> (Redemption 's opening cinematic suggests that Christof was Embraced in 1141 CE. The game's timeline presents several inconsistencies with both in-setting and real-world history -- such as Christof's own sire, Ecaterina, not being Embraced until 1150. The 1194 date listed in VTM: Beckett's Jyhad Diary is probably the more accurate.)<br /> So he was/is of 9th Gen (possibly 8th if diablerizing the Setite Lucretia)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T12:31:58-07:00","id":1509614,"title":"","content":"Thanks Shadowprowler.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T16:31:01-07:00","id":1509640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Christof Romuald</b>\u200b was Embraced by Ecaterina the Wise, in Prague during the Dark Ages. She was originally an eighth generation vampire, but committed diablerie in the late 20th century.<br /> (Redemption 's opening cinematic suggests that Christof was Embraced in 1141 CE. The game's timeline presents several inconsistencies with both in-setting and real-world history -- such as Christof's own sire, Ecaterina, not being Embraced until 1150. The 1194 date listed in VTM: Beckett's Jyhad Diary is probably the more accurate.)<br /> So he was/is of 9th Gen (possibly 8th if diablerizing the Setite Lucretia)\u200b </div> </div> </div>Yes, it's hard to be sure about anything regarding Cristof, because he came from a PC game and in the game many things are changed/different from the established lore of the WoD. The date of his embrace is just one among these many of these discrepancies, another being Ecaterina's embrace, also the fact that she seems way too powerful to have been embraced only some decades before embracing Cristof (not to mention her telekinesis shenanigans, that always made me and my friends, kids at the time we played the game, spend hours wondering what she did), the Methuselah in Prague in the game is known as Vukodlak, but is known as Shaagra in vampire books and is a &quot;she&quot; (even though gender in vampire is something definitely not that relevant, ESPECIALLY for a Tzimisce who could change completely in a blink of an eye). Not to forget the fact you face Etrius in his own chantry and not only isn't destroyed, but also give the Tremere Councillor quite a beating lol.<br /> <br /> To sum up, all in all the game differs a lot from the books, so it's hard to say what is &quot;true&quot; there and in this case I'd normally prefer to take the information found in Becket's Diary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-27T15:10:24-07:00","id":1509900,"title":"","content":"It certainly sounds like a mystery about this Brujah and maybe my Malkavian should look into it.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-27T19:32:38-07:00","id":1509915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508001-eye-of-hazimel?p=1509900#post1509900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It certainly sounds like a mystery about this Brujah and maybe my Malkavian should look into it.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I also feel the need to advertise the game, for all its problems it's an interesting game and one of the few set in the Dark Ages and Vampire the Masquerade Scenario. Til this day, there is a loyal community who releases mods for it. I find it quite interesting, even if the stories can be at times absurd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-27T21:47:44-07:00","id":1509918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508001-eye-of-hazimel?p=1509640#post1509640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, it's hard to be sure about anything regarding Cristof, because he came from a PC game and in the game many things are changed/different from the established lore of the WoD. The date of his embrace is just one among these many of these discrepancies, another being Ecaterina's embrace, also the fact that she seems way too powerful to have been embraced only some decades before embracing Cristof (not to mention her telekinesis shenanigans, that always made me and my friends, kids at the time we played the game, spend hours wondering what she did), the Methuselah in Prague in the game is known as Vukodlak, but is known as Shaagra in vampire books and is a &quot;she&quot; (even though gender in vampire is something definitely not that relevant, ESPECIALLY for a Tzimisce who could change completely in a blink of an eye). Not to forget the fact you face Etrius in his own chantry and not only isn't destroyed, but also give the Tremere Councillor quite a beating lol.<br /> <br /> To sum up, all in all the game differs a lot from the books, so it's hard to say what is &quot;true&quot; there and in this case I'd normally prefer to take the information found in Becket's Diary.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think Vukodlak and Shaagra are meant to be the same character.<br /> <br /> It's one replacing the other as Lord of Prague.<br /> <br /> But since Vukdolak has been imprisoned under a Tzimisce ritual, it's not necessarily a contradiction.<br /> <br /> As for defeating Etrius, well, he's only a couple of centuries old vampire. 4th generation or not. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-28T09:58:18-07:00","id":1509967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508001-eye-of-hazimel?p=1509918#post1509918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think Vukodlak and Shaagra are meant to be the same character.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed<br /> Vukodlak dwelled amongst the Antediluvians before the Deluge and commenced to defile and twist the fabric and essences of all that was good and fair in the now cleansed Earth... and died in 2000 CE<br /> While Shaagra was a Tzimisce Methuselah who rested under the city of Prague and she was Embraced in 152 CE and finally met her end during World War II when her haven was hit by a bomb and she burned to ashes in February 14, 1945 CE<br /> This theory about Shaagra and Vukodlak is the same was born from the fact that Vukodlak was served by Libussa, who was Shaagra's ghoul according to Transylvania by Night.<br /> But thats hardly a &quot;proof&quot;, Libussa easly could have found a new Master after Shaagra's Final Death...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 04-28-2023, 01:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-28T18:04:33-07:00","id":1510006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508001-eye-of-hazimel?p=1509918#post1509918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think Vukodlak and Shaagra are meant to be the same character.<br /> <br /> It's one replacing the other as Lord of Prague.<br /> <br /> But since Vukdolak has been imprisoned under a Tzimisce ritual, it's not necessarily a contradiction.<br /> <br /> As for defeating Etrius, well, he's only a couple of centuries old vampire. 4th generation or not. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Age is definitely not a very relevant thing regarding exceptional kindreds like Etrius, Goratrix and co, as a matter of fact not really in Vampire at all when we take into consideration <i>diablerie</i> and other things like comparing different characters sheets with the same age, but with these we have a more or less clear view of their capabilities, Etrius would have already Thaumaturgy 8 or 9 (depending on the source) and maestry over all known paths and that alone being in his own chantry he would likely obliterate a band of neonates in few seconds. Even though he isn't really beaten in the game, but rather decides he has more relevant things to do than deal with them, it's still far-fetched lol (not to mention the fact that they invade the chantry killing dozens of Tremere on their way, but we could attribute that to the fact that it's a PC game).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-28T18:43:05-07:00","id":1510009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508001-eye-of-hazimel?p=1510006#post1510006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Age is definitely not a very relevant thing regarding exceptional kindreds like Etrius, Goratrix and co, as a matter of fact not really in Vampire at all when we take into consideration <i>diablerie</i> and other things like comparing different characters sheets with the same age, but with these we have a more or less clear view of their capabilities, Etrius would have already Thaumaturgy 8 or 9 (depending on the source) and maestry over all known paths and that alone being in his own chantry he would likely obliterate a band of neonates in few seconds. Even though he isn't really beaten in the game, but rather decides he has more relevant things to do than deal with them, it's still far-fetched lol (not to mention the fact that they invade the chantry killing dozens of Tremere on their way, but we could attribute that to the fact that it's a PC game).</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends on how you want to portray them. At the end of the day, I believe they never stated Etrius for a reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-28T22:10:06-07:00","id":1510031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508001-eye-of-hazimel?p=1510009#post1510009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It depends on how you want to portray them. At the end of the day, I believe they never stated Etrius for a reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe the only reason is what I believe is a wrong one, to not say &quot;sheer laziness&quot; or &quot;coincidence&quot;. In any case, beyond the fact that this phrase could be said about really any character in the game, if one wants to give Baba Yaga Thaumaturgy 6 instead of 9, it's up to them, but it wouldn't make much sense, in any case, in the end it's ALWAYS up to the ST.<br /> Etrius was quite formidable in his own rights and I believe they didn't give him traits because they thought it wasn't necessary, his text in Transylvania Chronicles: I, reads as: <i><b>No stats are given for Etrius. Should the characters attempt to go toe-to-toe with him, they deserve the painful, lingering deaths they receive. Feel free to give Etrius any Thaumaturgical powers and rituals (save those only available to Tremere himself) he may need. His basic attributes are all 4 or better and he possesses Iron Will.</b> </i>So, it's clear in his text that he should be quite beyond the powers of a small group of neonates. The only reason he doesn't have a character is that they didn't think it was worth the effort (and quite frankly, making a character sheet like this is quite a word count and a pain in the ass, but in my opinion a necessary one). At least we got a stated Goratrix and as both have a similar level of power, it's not that hard to imagine how Etrius character sheet would look like.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't think Vukodlak and Shaagra are meant to be the same character. </div> </div> </div>They may not have meant to, but it's quite a &quot;coincidence&quot; we have both characters with so much in common.<br /> <br /> In any case, I think we have derailed a lot from the theme here. I quite liked the idea of the &quot;Eye of Odin&quot;, it sounds very cool.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-29T10:08:32-07:00","id":1510104,"title":"","content":"Oh yes Marcus Vitel coming back would cast light on Theo Bell's skill and loyalty as a Archon for the Camarilla CT Phipps. I'm sure that the Inner Circle were quite happy to see Hardstadt meet his final death. I just hope that they will flesh out on why they didn't put the Brujah on the Red List in later books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-29T10:34:18-07:00","id":1510109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It depends on how you want to portray them. At the end of the day, I believe they never stated Etrius for a reason. </div> </div> </div>In any case, this phrase could be said about really any character in the game, if one wants to give Baba Yaga Thaumaturgy 6 instead of 9, it's up to them, but it wouldn't make much sense, in any case, in the end it's ALWAYS up to the ST.<br /> Etrius was quite formidable in his own rights and I believe they didn't give him traits because they thought it wasn't necessary, his text in Transylvania Chronicles: I, reads as: <i><b>No stats are given for Etrius. Should the characters attempt to go toe-to-toe with him, they deserve the painful, lingering deaths they receive. Feel free to give Etrius any Thaumaturgical powers and rituals (save those only available to Tremere himself) he may need. His basic attributes are all 4 or better and he possesses Iron Will.</b> </i>So, it's clear in his text that he should be quite beyond the powers of a small group of neonates. The only reason he doesn't have a character is that they didn't think it was worth the effort (and quite frankly, making a character sheet like this is quite a word count and a pain in the ass, but in my opinion a necessary one). At least we got a stated Goratrix and as both have a similar level of power, it's not that hard to imagine how Etrius character sheet would look like.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Indeed<br /> Vukodlak dwelled amongst the Antediluvians before the Deluge and commenced to defile and twist the fabric and essences of all that was good and fair in the now cleansed Earth... and died in 2000 CE<br /> While Shaagra was a Tzimisce Methuselah who rested under the city of Prague and she was Embraced in 152 CE and finally met her end during World War II when her haven was hit by a bomb and she burned to ashes in February 14, 1945 CE<br /> This theory about Shaagra and Vukodlak is the same was born from the fact that Vukodlak was served by Libussa, who was Shaagra's ghoul according to Transylvania by Night.<br /> But thats hardly a &quot;proof&quot;, Libussa easly could have found a new Master after Shaagra's Final Death...\u200b </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't think Vukodlak and Shaagra are meant to be the same character.<br /> <br /> It's one replacing the other as Lord of Prague.<br /> <br /> But since Vukdolak has been imprisoned under a Tzimisce ritual, it's not necessarily a contradiction.<br /> \u200b </div> </div> </div>They are perhaps not meant to be the same character and in this case I didn't mean it was necessarily a contradiction, but rather that they could be the same character in a &quot;different light&quot;, i.e. in a PC game and in the books for the tabletop RPG. I just think there are too many &quot;coincidences&quot;, so that it's perhaps easier to think they are the same character expressed through different &quot;medias&quot;.<br /> <br /> PS: I don't know what it happening with my posts, sometimes I get a message saying the post was &quot;unauthorized&quot; and I don't know if it's available for everyone to read them, that's why I repeated some things I wrote in the post that was labeled &quot;unauthorized&quot; for some reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}